=== corrected, deeper root cause (supersedes earlier 'stuck coordinator' guesses) ===
Every consumer-group hiccup across R11-01/05/08 traces to ONE real cause: our minimal
consumer.py does not handle SIGTERM gracefully (no consumer.close() / explicit LeaveGroup).
docker stop sends SIGTERM then SIGKILL after the grace period, but kafka-python never gets
a chance to tell the broker it's leaving - so the broker only notices via heartbeat
expiration, which takes up to the full session timeout (~40s observed) before a rebalance
can complete and the new consumer instance actually gets its partition assignment and starts
receiving messages. This explains the apparent 'not processing yet' observations - the
backlog DID drain, just ~40s after restart, not immediately. A production consumer should
install a signal handler that calls consumer.close() to avoid this real, common delay.
